IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja2-part5-ca-criminal.l4: Part 5 (Court of Appeal), Division 3, Criminal jurisdiction: ss 60D and 60E.
-- Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering (SCJA1969.txt), not the official text. Layer 1: the law, objectively; every name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Criminal jurisdiction is encoded for the accused as the individual on whom the court acts; there is no seat export for it (PLAN.md, Part 2).
-- JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (scja2)").

§ `Part 5, Division 3 -- Criminal jurisdiction`

§§ `s 60D -- Criminal jurisdiction`

DECLARE `s 60D kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 60D(a) an appeal against a decision made by the General Division in the exercise of its original criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 60D(b) a petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60D(c) a review of a decision of the Court of Appeal, or a decision of the General Division, under Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60D(d) a case stated to the Court of Appeal under section 395 or 396 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60D(e) a reference to the Court of Appeal under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60D(f) a motion to the Court of Appeal under Division 5 of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60D(g) a reference to the Court of Appeal under section 18 of the Extradition Act 1968`
    `s 60D another kind of matter`

-- src:3384 | 60D. The criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal consists of
-- src:3385 | the following matters, subject to the provisions of this Act or any
-- src:3386 | other written law regulating the terms and conditions upon which
-- src:3387 | those matters may be brought:
-- src:3389 | (a) any appeal against any decision made by the General
-- src:3390 | Division in the exercise of its original criminal jurisdiction;
-- src:3392 | (b) any petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20
-- src:3393 | of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:3395 | (c) any review of a decision of the Court of Appeal, or a
-- src:3396 | decision of the General Division, under Division 1B of
-- src:3397 | Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:3399 | (d) any case stated to the Court of Appeal under section 395 or
-- src:3400 | 396 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:3407 | (e) any reference to the Court of Appeal under section 397 of
-- src:3408 | the Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:3410 | (f) any motion to the Court of Appeal under Division 5 of
-- src:3411 | Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:3417 | (g) any reference to the Court of Appeal under section 18 of
-- src:3418 | the Extradition Act 1968.
@ref s 60D (src:3384-3418)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 60D kind of matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 60D(a) an appeal against a decision made by the General Division in the exercise of its original criminal jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60D(b) a petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60D(c) a review of a decision of the Court of Appeal, or a decision of the General Division, under Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60D(d) a case stated to the Court of Appeal under section 395 or 396 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60D(e) a reference to the Court of Appeal under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60D(f) a motion to the Court of Appeal under Division 5 of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60D(g) a reference to the Court of Appeal under section 18 of the Extradition Act 1968` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal consists of the following matters" closes the list at paragraphs (a) to (g)
    WHEN `s 60D another kind of matter` THEN JUST FALSE

§§ `s 60E -- Composition when exercising criminal jurisdiction`

-- src:3424 | 60E.—(1) Despite section 50(1), a case before the Court of Appeal
-- src:3425 | may, if the Tenth Schedule so provides, be heard and determined by a
-- src:3426 | single Judge.
@ref s 60E(1) (src:3424-3426)
GIVEN `the number of Judges who hear and determine the case` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 10 the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` IS A MAYBE `Smaller panel`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 10 the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Tenth Schedule so provides is answered by another part of this encoding (PLAN.md seam 16)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Tenth Schedule so provides" -- the Schedule does not so provide, so the "if" is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05, part (b))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which panel the Tenth Schedule provides is answered by another part of this encoding (PLAN.md seam 16)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST panel THEN
            CONSIDER panel
            WHEN `a single Judge` THEN
                IF `the number of Judges who hear and determine the case` EQUALS 1
                THEN JUST TRUE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Tenth Schedule so provides" -- the Schedule provides for a single Judge, and this number is not one Judge
                ELSE JUST FALSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Tenth Schedule so provides, be heard and determined by a single Judge" -- the Schedule provides for another panel, not for a single Judge
            WHEN `a single Judge or 2 Judges` THEN JUST FALSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Tenth Schedule so provides, be heard and determined by a single Judge" -- the Schedule provides for another panel, not for a single Judge
            WHEN `2 Judges` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `s 60E(2) kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 60E(2)(a) an appeal against a conviction before the Judge or a sentence passed by the Judge`
    `s 60E(2)(b) a petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 lodged in respect of a sentence of death passed by the Judge on an accused`
    `s 60E(2)(c) a case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60E(2)(d) a reference under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 of a question of law of public interest that has arisen in a criminal matter determined by the Judge`
    `s 60E(2) a matter related to a matter in paragraphs (a) to (d)`
    `s 60E(2) another matter`

-- src:3430 | (2) A Judge must not sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide any
-- src:3431 | of the following matters, or any matter related to any of the following
-- src:3432 | matters:
-- src:3434 | (a) an appeal against a conviction before the Judge or a
-- src:3435 | sentence passed by the Judge;
-- src:3437 | (b) any petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20
-- src:3438 | of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 lodged in respect of a
-- src:3439 | sentence of death passed by the Judge on an accused;
-- src:3441 | (c) any case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the
-- src:3442 | Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:3444 | (d) any reference under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure
-- src:3445 | Code 2010 of a question of law of public interest that has
-- src:3446 | arisen in a criminal matter determined by the Judge.
@ref s 60E(2) (src:3430-3446)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 60E(2) kind of matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60E(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Judge must not sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide any of the following matters, or any matter related to any of the following matters"
    WHEN `s 60E(2)(a) an appeal against a conviction before the Judge or a sentence passed by the Judge` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): as above, paragraph (b)
    WHEN `s 60E(2)(b) a petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 lodged in respect of a sentence of death passed by the Judge on an accused` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): as above, paragraph (c)
    WHEN `s 60E(2)(c) a case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): as above, paragraph (d)
    WHEN `s 60E(2)(d) a reference under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 of a question of law of public interest that has arisen in a criminal matter determined by the Judge` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or any matter related to any of the following matters"
    WHEN `s 60E(2) a matter related to a matter in paragraphs (a) to (d)` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition reaches only the listed matters and matters related to them
    WHEN `s 60E(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING

-- The prohibition is derived from the answer above (ruling N2): the text names its bearer, "A Judge".
DECLARE `s 60E(2) party` IS ONE OF `s 60E(2) the Judge who dealt with the matter at first instance`
DECLARE `s 60E(2) act` IS ONE OF `s 60E(2) sits in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide a matter in paragraphs (a) to (d) or a matter related to it`

-- src:3430 | (2) A Judge must not sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide any
-- src:3431 | of the following matters, or any matter related to any of the following
-- src:3432 | matters:
-- src:3434 | (a) an appeal against a conviction before the Judge or a
-- src:3435 | sentence passed by the Judge;
-- src:3437 | (b) any petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20
-- src:3438 | of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 lodged in respect of a
-- src:3439 | sentence of death passed by the Judge on an accused;
-- src:3441 | (c) any case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the
-- src:3442 | Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:3444 | (d) any reference under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure
-- src:3445 | Code 2010 of a question of law of public interest that has
-- src:3446 | arisen in a criminal matter determined by the Judge.
@ref s 60E(2) (src:3430-3446)
`s 60E(2) the prohibition on the Judge` MEANS
    PARTY `s 60E(2) the Judge who dealt with the matter at first instance`
    SHANT `s 60E(2) sits in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide a matter in paragraphs (a) to (d) or a matter related to it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 60E(2) the Judge who dealt with the matter at first instance` BECAUSE "a Judge sat in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide a matter the Judge had dealt with at first instance, or a matter related to it"

#TRACE `s 60E(2) the prohibition on the Judge` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 60E(2) the Judge who dealt with the matter at first instance` DOES `s 60E(2) sits in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide a matter in paragraphs (a) to (d) or a matter related to it` AT 1
